## psc/sema/check/size.pengu — tipos de tamaño finito (E0050).
##
## Un rune (o echo) no puede contenerse a sí mismo por valor: el `struct` de C
## saldría con tamaño infinito. El chequeo recorre el grafo de "contiene por
## valor" y, cuando encuentra un ciclo, lo reporta con la cadena completa
## (`A -> B -> A`).
##
## Cubre las dos formas de crear un ciclo:
##
## - `fundere`: `rune A fundere A:` o `rune A fundere B:` + `rune B fundere A:`.
## - `cyclus` con un campo del propio tipo: `rune Node cyclus: next as Node`.
##
## La indirección rompe el ciclo: `ref to T`, `frozen ref to T`, `list of T`,
## `map of K to V`, `slice of T`, `many T` y los handles de `std.consortium`
## (`Rc`/`Arc`/`Weak`, que guardan un `ref` por dentro) no cuentan como
## contención por valor.
##
## ## Memoria
## Presta el programa; crea `SemaState` por módulo al diagnosticar.

insignia sema_size_

import std.builder

import psc.sema.ast as astutil
import psc.sema.diagnostics as sdiag
import psc.sema.modules.loader as loader
import psc.sema.modules.program as program
import psc.sema.names as npool
import psc.sema.state as state
import psc.sema.types.kind as tk
import psc.sema.types.table as types

## Color de un tipo en el DFS de tamaños.
const SIZE_UNVISITED as int is 0
const SIZE_ACTIVE as int is 1
const SIZE_DONE as int is 2

## Tope de profundidad; un ciclo real se detecta mucho antes.
const SIZE_MAX_DEPTH as int is 96

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API del pass
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Comprueba que ningún tipo nominal tenga tamaño infinito.
##
## ## Memoria
## Presta el programa; libera las listas temporales al terminar.
weave check_all_sizes with p as ref to program.SemaProgram into void:
    var n as int is calling types.type_count with (sigil of p->types)
    if n <= 1:
        return
    var color as vector of int is vector of int
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        calling color.push with SIZE_UNVISITED
        set i is i + 1
    var chain as vector of int is vector of int
    set i is 1
    while i < n:
        var t as tk.SemaType is calling types.at with (sigil of p->types), i
        if (t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkRune or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkEcho) and (color at i) == SIZE_UNVISITED:
            var ignored as bool is calling size_walk with p, (sigil of color), (sigil of chain), i, 0
        set i is i + 1
    banish chain
    banish color

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recorrido
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## ¿Este tipo contiene sus hijos por valor?
##
## ## Memoria
## Compara variantes; no asigna.
weave contains_by_value with t as tk.SemaType into bool:
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkBase:
        return false
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkRef or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkFrozen:
        return false
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkSlice or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkMany:
        return false
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkList or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkMap:
        return false
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkRange or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkFn:
        return false
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkOpaque or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkAny:
        return false
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkTypeParam:
        return false
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkNull or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkVoid:
        return false
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkError:
        return false
    return true

## Recorre un tipo y devuelve `true` si encuentra un ciclo.
##
## `chain` lleva la pila de nominales abiertos, en orden.
##
## ## Memoria
## Presta `color`/`chain`; no asigna.
weave size_walk with p as ref to program.SemaProgram, color as ref to vector of int, chain as ref to vector of int, ty as int, depth as int into bool:
    if ty <= 0 or depth > SIZE_MAX_DEPTH:
        return false
    if not (calling types.valid with (sigil of p->types), ty):
        return false
    var t as tk.SemaType is calling types.at with (sigil of p->types), ty
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkAlias or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkSeal:
        return calling size_walk with p, color, chain, t.b, depth + 1
    if not (calling contains_by_value with t):
        return false
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkRune or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkEcho or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkOmen:
        if (color at ty) == SIZE_ACTIVE:
            calling report_size_cycle with p, chain, ty
            return true
        if (color at ty) == SIZE_DONE:
            return false
        set color at ty is SIZE_ACTIVE
        calling chain->push with ty
        var found as bool is calling size_walk_children with p, color, chain, t, depth
        set color at ty is SIZE_DONE
        var ignored as int is calling chain->pop
        return found
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkArray:
        return calling size_walk with p, color, chain, t.a, depth + 1
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkMaybe or t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkResult:
        if calling size_walk with p, color, chain, t.a, depth + 1:
            return true
        return calling size_walk with p, color, chain, t.b, depth + 1
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkTuple:
        var i as int is 0
        var n as int is t.count
        while i < n:
            var c as int is calling types.type_child_at with (sigil of p->types), ty, i
            if calling size_walk with p, color, chain, c, depth + 1:
                return true
            set i is i + 1
    return false

## Recorre los campos (o el payload de cada variante) de un nominal.
##
## ## Memoria
## Presta `color`/`chain`; no asigna.
weave size_walk_children with p as ref to program.SemaProgram, color as ref to vector of int, chain as ref to vector of int, t as tk.SemaType, depth as int into bool:
    var info as types.SemaNominalInfo is (p->types.nominal_infos at t.a)
    if t.kind == tk.SemaTypeKind.TkOmen:
        var vi as int is 0
        while vi < info.variants_count:
            var v as types.SemaVariant is (p->types.variants at (info.variants_first + vi))
            var pj as int is 0
            while pj < v.payload_count:
                var pf as types.SemaField is (p->types.fields at (v.payload_first + pj))
                if calling size_walk with p, color, chain, pf.type, depth + 1:
                    return true
                set pj is pj + 1
            set vi is vi + 1
        return false
    var fi as int is 0
    while fi < info.fields_count:
        var f as types.SemaField is (p->types.fields at (info.fields_first + fi))
        if calling size_walk with p, color, chain, f.type, depth + 1:
            return true
        set fi is fi + 1
    return false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diagnóstico
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

## Reporta el ciclo `A -> B -> A` en la declaración del tipo que lo cierra.
##
## ## Memoria
## Crea un `SemaState` por módulo y strings owned; los libera.
weave report_size_cycle with p as ref to program.SemaProgram, chain as ref to vector of int, back as int into void:
    var bt as tk.SemaType is calling types.at with (sigil of p->types), back
    if bt.a < 0 or bt.a >= p->types.nominal_infos.len:
        return
    var info as types.SemaNominalInfo is (p->types.nominal_infos at bt.a)
    if info.module < 0 or info.module >= p->modules.len or info.decl_node < 0:
        return
    var start as int is 0
    var i as int is 0
    while i < chain->len:
        if (chain at i) == back:
            set start is i
            set i is chain->len
        else:
            set i is i + 1
    var sb as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    defer banish sb
    var j as int is start
    while j < chain->len:
        var ct as tk.SemaType is calling types.at with (sigil of p->types), (chain at j)
        var cn as string is calling npool.text with (sigil of p->names), ct.name
        calling sb.append with cn
        calling sb.append with " -> "
        set j is j + 1
    var bn as string is calling npool.text with (sigil of p->names), bt.name
    calling sb.append with bn
    var chaintext as string is calling sb.finish
    defer banish chaintext
    var m as loader.SemaModule is (p->modules at info.module)
    var st as state.SemaState is with program is p, module is (sigil of m), src is (sigil of m.source), lex is (sigil of m.lex), ast is (sigil of m.parse.ast), types is (sigil of p->types), symbols is (sigil of p->symbols), names is (sigil of p->names), bag is (sigil of p->diagnostics), opts is (sigil of p->options), annotations is (sigil of m.annotations), hooks is (calling state.default_hooks), errors is 0, max_errors is p->options.max_errors, stop_after_first is p->options.stop_after_first, stop is false, allow_mutating is false
    var msg as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    defer banish msg
    calling msg.append with "type '"
    calling msg.append with bn
    calling msg.append with "' has infinite size: "
    calling msg.append with chaintext
    var mtext as string is calling msg.finish
    defer banish mtext
    var help as StringBuilder is calling StringBuilder.new
    defer banish help
    calling help.append with "Break the cycle with 'ref to "
    calling help.append with bn
    calling help.append with "', 'list of "
    calling help.append with bn
    calling help.append with "', or an 'Rc'/'Arc' handle; a rune cannot contain itself by value."
    var htext as string is calling help.finish
    defer banish htext
    var start_off as int is calling astutil.start_of with (sigil of m.parse.ast), info.decl_node
    var end_off as int is calling astutil.end_of with (sigil of m.parse.ast), info.decl_node
    calling sdiag.node_error with st.bag, st.src, sdiag.CODE_INFINITE_SIZE, start_off, end_off, mtext, htext, ""
